type hazard is finding 1's `(<= deadline nil)`.\n\n**`ws_project.cljc` — `dial`.** Policy `select-keys` gains `give-up-after`; namespaced-key-only per spec; `dial-propagates-link-options` verifies all four link keys land on the link atom.\n\n**`dial-step!` multi-arity.** 1-arity delegates with nil and preserves existing callers exactly (no `:now`, no link step, nothing expires — `the-one-arity-dial-step-never-expires`). 2-arity: records `:now` on the dial, budgeted projection, link step **between** projection and mirror (correct: freshly deposited answers reach the link before the expiry scan), budgeted mirror once outside any atom update (`dial-mirror-effects-run-once-per-step` still guards this), then closes the ws handle when the step answers gone — `closable?`-checked and idempotent, so repeated post-loss ticks are safe"}]}}
