{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Even writing to the plan file is blocked (it seems this session is in a print mode without write permissions). Therefore, I'll submit the review directly within the response and note the intended file path. Since the deliverable is a report, I'll output it inline in its complete form.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Write permissions are blocked in this session too, so I can't save the file. The review is complete — here is the full report, ready to be saved to `collab/1791359934597-stream-s2c-review.qwen3.8-max.findings.md`:\n\n---\n\n# S2c review: request liveness & channel expiry (qwen3.8-max)\n\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2`, branch `stream-crossmachine-s2`, base `91ab84f7`, uncommitted changes under review: `src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc`, `src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc`, both test files, and both design docs.\n\nRead firsthand: both source files in full, the S2c test sections, `dao.stream.remote.md` §2.4 (Channel loss + Expiry), §2.5, §3.0, `dao.stream.ws.md` Deferred/Liveness, the architect spec (§1.2–§4), the S2c prompt and author report. Method note: shell and write access were blocked in this session, so `git diff` was not run; the review is against the full working-tree files, cross-checked line by line against every claim in the author report. All claimed edits and tests were located and verified.\n\n## Finding summary\n\n| # | Severity | Location | Description | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | P3 | `remote.cljc` `link-step!` (~1112–1129) | `(step cd nil)` erases a previously recorded `:now` and, once any entry carries a `:deadline`, throws on `(<= deadline nil)` on all three hosts. Unreachable via `dial-step!` (guarded by `some? now`), but `:step` is public API of `links`. | Guard `link-step!`: when `now` is nil, skip recording and skip the scan (or throw a composition error). |\n| 2 | P3 | deadline stamping; `ws_project.cljc` `establish!` | A request that first exists on the link **before any timed step never receives a deadline**, even after the driver starts stepping with `now`. The `establish!` fix covers only dials already stepped at a `now`; a driver that attaches first and steps later leaves the attach probe — the establishment stall Expiry bounds — undying. Follows the spec's letter (\"before any step with `now`, nothing is stamped\"); the spec is silent on backfill. | Record for the Architect: document that drivers must step with `now` before first attach/resolve, or amend the spec to backfill deadlines at the first timed step. Non-blocking for S2c; matters for the S3a driver. |\n| 3 | P4 | `remote.cljc` `send-named!` | `(new-deadline link)` computed twice in the `cond->`. Pure and correct under driver discipline, but fragile. | `let`-bind the deadline once. |\n| 4 | P4 | `remote.cljc` `channel-loss!` | `:pending` survives channel loss (author note 2, deliberately left). Inert per S2b sign-off, but a reflection that never closes retains its entry for the link's lifetime. | Optional hygiene: clear `:pending` in `channel-loss!`. Not required. |\n| 5 | P4 | tests | No test expires a **named** resolve request through `:step` (`send-named!`'s stamping path); only post-loss `resolve` → `channel-gone` is covered. | Add: unanswered named request, step at deadline, expiry. |\n\n## Detailed analysis\n\n**`remote.cljc` — policy.** `give-up-after` added to the `links` `select-keys` and to positive-integer-or-nil validation (`ex-info \"invalid DaoStream remote link policy\"`); `new-link` stores it plus `:now nil`. Tested with 0, −1, 1.5. Matches spec §1.2/§1.3.\n\n**`new-deadline`.** `(+ now give-up-after)`, nil when either is missing — clock-less compositions stamp nothing. Arithmetic is portable (int+int and mixed comparison are clean on JVM/CLJS/Dart; epoch-ms magnitudes are far below any precision boundary).\n\n**Stamping discipline**, verified on every path: accepted sends stamp via `register!` (`send-request!`, `refl-append`, `send-named!`); kept probes carry their original deadline because `send-request!` does the **pending lookup first** — never restamped on retry or eventual send (verified in `a-kept-probe-has-a-deadline`); waiting `:probe` entries are unstamped until `admit-probe!`; `count-ask!` touches only `:asks`, never `:deadline`; `absorb!`/`absorb-named!` remove the entry, deadline included. All exactly per spec.\n\n**`link-step!` / `:step`.** Order matches the spec: record `:now`, budgeted `drain!`, then — skipped when `channel-gone?` is already true, so an `end`-loss in the same step doesn't double-report — scan `(concat outstanding pending)` for the least id with `:deadline <= now`, emit `channel-expired` (id, op), run `channel-loss!` (abandons outstanding, `append-unknown` per append, sets gone). Return shape `{:dao.stream.remote/channel-gone? bool :dao.stream.remote/expired id-or-nil}`; nil for unreached channels. Drain-before-scan is the right ordering: an answer arriving in the deadline's own tick clears its entry before the scan. `:step` creating the link on a reached-but-unattached channel via `link-for!` is harmless and pre-records `:now`. Only gaps: findings 1–2.\n\n**Flood immunity.** The scan is independent of drain-budget; `flood-cannot-defer-expiry` (budget 2, 60 junk values) demonstrates the accepted D3 trade-off (possible false loss, never deferred expiry).\n\n**Memory.** No new leak: `:outstanding` cleared on loss; `:filed`/`:filed-cursors` bounded by `max-filed` (S2b); `:pending` retention is pre-existing and bounded by `max-outstanding` when composed (finding 4). Expired entries can't accumulate — expiry is whole-channel loss and all send paths guard on `channel-gone?`.\n\n**Portability.** No reader conditionals needed: `some->`, `concat`, `sort-by key`, numeric `<=` are clj/cljs/cljd-safe. No side effects inside `swap!` in the new paths (`emit!`/`channel-loss!` run outside swaps). The only reachable type hazard is finding 1's `(<= deadline nil)`.\n\n**`ws_project.cljc` — `dial`.** Policy `select-keys` gains `give-up-after`; namespaced-key-only per spec; `dial-propagates-link-options` verifies all four link keys land on the link atom.\n\n**`dial-step!` multi-arity.** 1-arity delegates with nil and preserves existing callers exactly (no `:now`, no link step, nothing expires — `the-one-arity-dial-step-never-expires`). 2-arity: records `:now` on the dial, budgeted projection, link step **between** projection and mirror (correct: freshly deposited answers reach the link before the expiry scan), budgeted mirror once outside any atom update (`dial-mirror-effects-run-once-per-step` still guards this), then closes the ws handle when the step answers gone — `closable?`-checked and idempotent, so repeated post-loss ticks are safe. Nil `stepped` is falsy in the gone-check — no spurious close.\n\n**`establish!`.** Stores `:cd`/`:step!` and, when the dial has a recorded `now`, steps the new link before any probe exists — since `:step` creates the link via `link-for!`, the later `:attach` reuses it with `:now` set, so the immediately-sent attach probe is stamped. This is the one beyond-the-letter behavior; the rationale is sound and the mechanism verified. Residual gap is finding 2.\n\n**Tests.** All seven required `remote_test` cases and both `ws_project_test` cases exist and assert the right things, plus the two S2b follow-ups. Highlights verified: exact event sequence in `a-request-past-its-deadline-is-channel-loss` (`channel-expired` id 0 op descriptor, then `append-unknown`), exact step return maps at 9/10, `next`/`cursor`/`resolve` → `channel-gone` not retryable, `descriptor` still `ok`; the full teardown chain in `dial-step-with-now-closes-the-handle-on-expiry` (handle open at 9, closed at 10, `:ws/closed` closes projection and ring, resolve answers `channel-gone`). Fixtures are consistent with file style. Gap: finding 5.\n\n**Docs.** §2.4 names expiry as a loss cause; the Expiry paragraph matches the implementation exactly (contract, return shape, all stamping rules, resend immobility, answer clearing, clock-less default, liveness framing, flood caveat, dial handle close). §2.5 keeps \"the reflection reads no clock\" true, adds the UDP note. §3.0 gains the Request-liveness bullet. `dao.stream.ws.md` Deferred/Liveness points at remote §2.4. No drift between doc text and code.\n\n**Author report cross-check.** Every claim located in the tree, including the three review notes. The reported runs (83 tests / 609 assertions, cljstyle clean, kondo 0 errors with the pre-existing `peer2` warning) could not be re-executed here — re-run `clojure -M:test -n dao.stream.remote-test -n dao.stream.ws-project-test` before landing.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**ACCEPT.**\n\nThe slice implements architect spec §1.2/§1.3 (S2c rows), the §2 failure table, §3 test plan and §4 doc amendments faithfully; stamping, resend immobility, answer clearing, expiry-scan ordering and dial teardown are correct and well-tested, with no portability or memory regressions. Findings 1–5 are non-blocking: 1 is a one-line robustness guard on a path the shipped composition never takes; 2 is a spec-silent ordering question for the Architect record and S3a; 3–5 are hygiene. Recommend landing as one commit (`feat(dao.stream.remote): request deadlines, channel-expired and link step (cross-machine stream slice S2c)`) after re-running the test lanes, tracking findings 1, 2 and 5 as follow-ups.\n\n---"}]}}
